Z||000002||fierospeeder||09-24-2001||04:23 AM||||same with monkeyman  315 am<P>i seen a guy selling 89 front disc brakes on ebay about last year.  They were rusted but brand new with a stock number tag.<P>Its sort of a touchy topic.  Did gm have parts to go on the new 89 fiero, but production was halted.  And some of the workers grabbed the parts.  Or the parts were used on different cars??<P>We need a forum member that works with GM, and someone from the production line that built the fiero for all the years it was being made.  So we can know the Real Truth.||||reg||1
Z||000003||007DOUG||09-24-2001||07:01 AM||||That's Joe Wynman selling, and those are 89 links.<P>Joe has sold a pair on ebay before. If my memory is good, they went for an unholy $700+<P>Joe has managed to rescue alot of rare fiero parts. Such as 89 rotors, these swaybar links, and the Master VIN list for all Indys produced.<P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top. IRM car<BR>86 GT Red<BR>86 GT Yellow ASAP<BR>86 GT Pearl White 3.4 T-top<BR>88 Coupe Red<BR>88 Formula Red 5 speed<BR>88 GT Black leather<BR>88 GT Black lumbar<BR>88 GT Black 3.4, 5 speed, T-top<P><BR>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||14
Z||000004||Boomtastic||09-24-2001||08:57 AM||||These are not the only pair in existence. Recently I've had the chance to see, hold, and examine a set and they are exactly what he describes. They were reported to be 1989 pieces, and billed as they only pieces for the 1989 Fiero to have made production. They are VERY light and have yellow urethane bushings on either end. I have no reason to doubt that they are not from the 1989 Fiero. But then again, there are those that say my 1989 prototype emblems aren't legit ..<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
